Z||000000||RossT||05-15-2001||01:21 AM||||Well I have been searching for another fiero for a while and have narrowed the search down to 3-4 cars. My ultimate car (after 88gt t-tops) has always been the blue 87gt then the 85gt. Since Vinnywolf and fierodave2001 have refused to sell their blue gt's to me, I had to look elsewhere(joking). I have found a couple of decent blue gt's.  This one is by far in the best shape but the original (current) onwer decided to paint the original rare 87gt a BMW shade of blue.  Almost looks like fierolisa's car.  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/car5.jpg"> <P>less than 47,000 miles too.. <P>Mrfiero is looking at another car that I am interested in also.<P>Will post a pic of that car later.||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||05-15-2001||01:28 AM||||I told you my opinion of blue Fieros (I think the factory electric blue is too bright), but I sort of like the darker blue.  It's too bad it doesn't have a spoiler.....I think the GT looks better with one, but that's my opinion.<P>I will be taking those pictures of the '85 GT tomorrow, so you should get them by the end of the week.<P><BR> ||||reg||1
